<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Generality Lands</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Generality Lands were territories of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a> governed directly by the States General rather than forming provinces of their own. Conquered mainly from the Spanish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> during the Eighty Years' War, they included <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/states-brabant">States Brabant</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zeelandic-flanders">States Flanders</a> and parts of Limburg and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-guelders">Upper Guelders</a>. Their largely Catholic inhabitants had no vote in the States General, and the lands correspond broadly to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-brabant">North Brabant</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> Limburg.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/generality-lands.jpg" alt="Generality Lands" width="320" height="363" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Joostik · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Republiek_der_Zeven_Verenigde_Nederlanden.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
